The build succeeded. Here's a summary of what was implemented:

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- The C API follows the **ABI boundary pattern**: the opaque `fmt_args_t*` pointer is defined in the `.cc` file only, so C callers never see C++ types — the header is valid as a pure C include
- Unlike `printf`, type information is encoded **in the push function call** (`fmt_push_int`, `fmt_push_cstr`, etc.) rather than in format string characters (`%d`, `%s`), making the API type-safe even with runtime format strings
- `fmt_format_to` wraps exceptions in a `try/catch(...)` block because C callers have no stack-unwinding mechanism — returning `-1` is the only safe error signal across the C/C++ ABI boundary
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

## Files created/modified

**`include/fmt/c.h`** (new) — Pure C header, includes under `extern "C"`:
- `fmt_args_t*` opaque handle + `fmt_args_new()` / `fmt_args_free()`
- 9 typed push functions: `fmt_push_int`, `fmt_push_uint`, `fmt_push_long_long`, `fmt_push_ulong_long`, `fmt_push_double`, `fmt_push_bool`, `fmt_push_cstr`, `fmt_push_str`, `fmt_push_pointer`
- `fmt_format_to(buf, n, fmt_str, args)` — snprintf-style (returns total chars, NUL-terminates)

**`src/fmt-c.cc`** (new) — C++ implementation wrapping `dynamic_format_arg_store<context>` and `detail::vformat_to`

**`CMakeLists.txt`** (modified) — Added `c.h` to `FMT_HEADERS` and `src/fmt-c.cc` to `FMT_SOURCES`

